  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c73bcde73ca45b24c870219573f99a55, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The flower stall on the residential row. Funerals, mostly. Lilies. I closed early to come home.
    midDaysAnswer: The stall. There are no flowers left to sell. I arranged the empty buckets. Then I walked home.
    finalDaysAnswer: The stall. Or where it used to be. I stood there for a while. Then I came here.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The bakery on Lenina Street. I work the ovens there. Six years now.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My new flat. I only moved to the residential block last week. I am still unpacking.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: From home. My husband walked me to the corner. We have been married for many years.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. I remember procedures very well. Other things I lose sometimes. That is not a symptom.
    midDaysAnswer: I lose small things. Keys. Days. I do not sleep much. I wait up. I feel fine.
    finalDaysAnswer: I am a little tired. I have been waiting a long time. That is all it is.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: No. My memory is perfect. I have never lost anything in my life. Not one thing.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Only a stiff neck from the dress. I bought it on Monday. I had never worn it before this week.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing. I am not waiting for anything. There is no wedding. There never was.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - I know you are not supposed to ask about the dress. Most people do not ask.
    - There is a ceremony soon. I am told to stay ready. So I stay ready.
    - I have been through this checkpoint many times. You get used to the smell.
    midDays:
    - The dress holds its shape well. Considering. I have had it a long time.
    - I once asked someone here what day it was. He told me. It was not the day I thought it was.
    - I do not mind waiting. I have been waiting for quite a while now. A little longer is nothing.
    finalDays:
    - Do you think it will rain? I cannot get the dress very wet. I have already had it cleaned once.
    - Everyone always looks at the dress first. I understand. It is a very white dress.
    - I have been counting the days. I stopped when I lost count. It was a high number.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
